course: dictionary
lesson: 15674
title: Tiara: a small crown
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A tiara is a small crown, often decorated with jewels. «Mia wore a sparkly tiara to her birthday party.» The words sparkly and party are clues: a tiara is shiny and special, and people wear it on a happy day.
explain: Look for clues about who wears it. «The princess put on her diamond tiara for the royal ball.» Princess, royal and ball tell you a tiara is worn at important events. Ask yourself what would fit in the sentence: crown would fit, so a tiara is a kind of crown.
explain: Context can also show an older meaning. «Long ago, popes wore a tall tiara with three crowns.» Popes and long ago are the clues, so this tiara is not a party crown. It is a tall crown from church history.
fact: A tiara is a small crown, often decorated with jewels.
fact: Women and girls wear tiaras at special events, such as birthdays, weddings and balls.
fact: «A sparkly tiara» and «a diamond tiara» describe what a tiara looks like or what it is decorated with.
fact: The papal tiara was a tall triple crown once worn by popes.
fact: When you meet a new word, check the words around it. Tiara sits near words like crown, princess and jewels, so it is a crown.
exercise: «Mia wore a sparkly tiara to her birthday party.» What is a tiara? | A pair of shiny shoes | A large hat for the sun | A type of birthday cake | *A small crown, often decorated with jewels
exercise: Who usually wears a tiara? | Dogs and cats | Only men who work in offices | *Women and girls, like princesses and queens | Children who are ill in bed
exercise: What does triple mean in «The papal tiara was a tall triple crown»? | Only one | Very cheap | Very shiny | *Three, as in three crowns stacked together
test: Which best describes a tiara? | A large boat for the sea | A kind of shoe worn for running | *A small crown decorated with jewels | A type of bread
test: In «Long ago, popes wore a tall tiara with three crowns», what kind of tiara is meant? | A sparkly one for a birthday girl | *The tall, old crown worn by popes in church history | A small paper one made at school | A toy one for dressing up
exam: When a princess wears a tiara at a royal ball, what does tiara mean? | *A small crown, often decorated with jewels | A kind of cake | A cloth worn round the neck | A long, thin spoon
